both
46. Systemd Boundary

Systemd remains responsible for OS/process lifecycle where appropriate:

start Pantheon
restart Pantheon after failure
boot activation

Zodiac should not replace systemd.

The established daemon already runs under the user systemd boundary.

Application-level recurrence belongs to Zodiac.

47. Transition from Cron/Hermes

Do not cut over every schedule simultaneously without evidence.

For applicable legacy Hermes cron jobs:

inventory existing schedule;
create equivalent Zodiac declaration;
overlap read-only/non-conflicting observation where safe for approximately 1–2 days;
compare actual runs/results;
ensure no duplicate consequential delivery;
pause the replaced Hermes job;
verify paused state;
preserve rollback.

Do not uninstall Hermes yet.

48. Avoid Duplicate Briefs

During overlap, never allow both Hermes and Zodiac/Pantheon to email the same daily brief.

Use shadow execution or disable external delivery on one side.

A double-send is a failed cutover, not harmless duplication.

