51. Authority at Due Time

A schedule declaration does not necessarily guarantee the consequential operation is authorized forever.

At due time:

Zodiac due instance
        ↓
normal authority path
        ↓
Future
        ↓
Mercury
        ↓
Bifrost/local deterministic capability

Use standing authority where explicitly granted.

If authority is missing:

Needs You

or an approval state.

Do not silently fail and mark complete.

52. Prometheus

Prometheus governs Zodiac-triggered execution.

If Pantheon is paused:

Zodiac may calculate time/state;
it must not dispatch new consequential autonomous work;
due instances should become appropriately blocked/deferred according to policy;
resume must not automatically replay everything.

Apply each schedule’s catch-up policy after resume.

