81. Schedule Mutation History

Preserve correction history for schedule declarations.

The foundational correction rule says earlier records should not simply disappear when corrected.

For consequential changes preserve:

previous value
new value
source of correction
time
reason where known

Do not keep an unbounded noisy event stream if a compact revision ledger satisfies this.

82. Schedule Disable vs Delete

Prefer disabling/retiring recurring declarations rather than hard deletion where historical traceability matters.

Support an explicit state such as:

disabled
completed
retired

